      "content": "I understand you are in pain, but I cannot advise you to self-medicate when you have ongoing stomach issues. Even low doses of ibuprofen still have the potential to cause gastric irritation, especially when combined with long-term acid suppression. If you absolutely must take something, try acetaminophen first, as it is much less harsh on the stomach. If the tooth pain is unbearable, consider an ice pack on the outside of your cheek for immediate relief while you plan to speak with a professional.",
